{
  "assessment": "The paper provides a quantitative model for the static rolling friction of liquid marbles, with explicit equations, fitted parameters, and experimental data across multiple regimes. It supports extraction of mechanisms, controls (marble volume, surface fraction), readouts (departure angle, static friction, curvature difference, raft yielding force), and quantitative claims with uncertainties. The source is suitable for authoring an interactive experiment.",
  "case_authoring_ready": true,
  "source": {
    "citation": "Yui Takai, Static Friction of Liquid Marbles, Physical Review Letters (2026), DOI:10.1103/njnj-yhc6",
    "journal_doi": "10.1103/njnj-yhc6",
    "arxiv_versioned_id": "2506.20116v2"
  },
  "paper_scope": "The paper investigates the static rolling friction of liquid marbles (water droplets coated with lycopodium particles) on tilted substrates. It develops a model based on shear yielding of the granular shell, validates it against departure-angle measurements for varying marble volume and particle surface fraction, and extends the logistic form of the intergrain force function to two-dimensional granular rafts. The study covers marble volumes from 1.5 to 300 µL, surface fractions from about 0.65 to near 1, and raft experiments with lycopodium and glass beads.",
  "mechanisms": [
    {
      "mechanism_id": "rolling_friction_energy_balance",
      "statement": "The onset of rolling of a liquid marble is governed by an energy balance: the gravitational energy gain during rolling must exceed the shear dissipation in the granular shell. The shell is modeled as a purely plastic, quasi-static granular raft with a cohesionless Mohr-Coulomb yield criterion.",
      "equations": [
        "δE_g ≈ ρ g Ω α δx",
        "δE_d ~ S d q_y δϵ",
        "q_y = μ p(φ)",
        "γ_eff = γ - p(φ) d = γ(1 - f(φ))",
        "α ≈ (S a^2 / Ω) (δϵ/δx) μ f(φ)/(1-f(φ))"
      ],
      "variable_names": [
        "α",
        "Ω",
        "ρ",
        "g",
        "δx",
        "S",
        "d",
        "q_y",
        "μ",
        "p(φ)",
        "γ_eff",
        "γ",
        "f(φ)",
        "a"
      ],
      "parameters": [
        {
          "name": "mu_large_marbles",
          "value": 0.053,
          "uncertainty": "±0.003 (standard error from fit)",
          "unit": "dimensionless",
          "role": "Macroscopic friction coefficient of the granular shell, fitted from large-marble departure angles.",
          "anchors": [
            {
              "line_start": 115,
              "line_end": 115,
              "support": "Fitting Eq. (model_large) in the large-marble regime with f(φ_o)=0.26 and a(φ_o)≈2.3 mm gives μ=0.053±0.003."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "f_phi_o",
          "value": 0.26,
          "uncertainty": "Not specified",
          "unit": "dimensionless",
          "role": "Dimensionless intergrain force function at the initial surface fraction φ_o=0.83.",
          "anchors": [
            {
              "line_start": 115,
              "line_end": 115,
              "support": "Fitting Eq. (model_large) with f(φ_o)=0.26 and a(φ_o)≈2.3 mm."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "a_phi_o",
          "value": 0.0023,
          "uncertainty": "Not specified",
          "unit": "m",
          "role": "Capillary length at φ_o, corresponding to γ_eff(φ_o)≈53 mN/m.",
          "anchors": [
            {
              "line_start": 115,
              "line_end": 115,
              "support": "a(φ_o)≈2.3 mm, i.e. γ_eff(φ_o)≈53 mN/m."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "anchors": [
        {
          "line_start": 87,
          "line_end": 89,
          "support": "Energy balance: δE_g≈ρgΩαδx exceeds shear dissipation δE_d~S d q_y δϵ; shell rheology modeled as purely plastic and quasi-static."
        },
        {
          "line_start": 90,
          "line_end": 91,
          "support": "Mohr-Coulomb criterion q_y=μp(φ); effective surface tension γ_eff=γ-p(φ)d."
        },
        {
          "line_start": 93,
          "line_end": 95,
          "support": "p(φ)=γf(φ)/d, so γ_eff=γ(1-f(φ))."
        },
        {
          "line_start": 96,
          "line_end": 99,
          "support": "Substituting into energy balance gives α≈(S a^2/Ω)(δϵ/δx) μ f(φ)/(1-f(φ))."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "mechanism_id": "large_marble_model",
      "statement": "For large marbles flattened by gravity to height ≈2a, the departure angle is given by a closed-form expression involving the capillary length, marble volume, and the intergrain force function.",
      "equations": [
        "Ω ≈ π l^2 a / 2",
        "S ≈ π l^2/2 + 2π l a",
        "δϵ ≈ δx / (2a)",
        "α ≈ (1/2) (1 + sqrt(8π a^3 / Ω)) μ f(φ)/(1-f(φ))"
      ],
      "variable_names": [
        "α",
        "Ω",
        "a",
        "l",
        "S",
        "δϵ",
        "δx",
        "μ",
        "f(φ)"
      ],
      "parameters": [],
      "anchors": [
        {
          "line_start": 105,
          "line_end": 107,
          "support": "Large-marble regime: height ≈2a, Ω≈πl^2a/2, S≈πl^2/2+2πla, δϵ≈δx/2a."
        },
        {
          "line_start": 109,
          "line_end": 113,
          "support": "Combining gives α≈(1/2)(1+sqrt(8πa^3/Ω)) μ f(φ)/(1-f(φ))."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "mechanism_id": "small_marble_model",
      "statement": "For small, quasi-spherical marbles, shear is confined near the contact region, leading to a different scaling of the departure angle with volume.",
      "equations": [
        "Ω ≈ 4π R^3 / 3",
        "l ~ R^2 / a",
        "S ≈ 2π R l",
        "δϵ ≈ δx / l",
        "α ≈ (6π^2)^{1/3} (a^3/Ω)^{2/3} μ f(φ)/(1-f(φ))"
      ],
      "variable_names": [
        "α",
        "Ω",
        "R",
        "a",
        "l",
        "S",
        "δϵ",
        "δx",
        "μ",
        "f(φ)"
      ],
      "parameters": [
        {
          "name": "small_marble_prefactor",
          "value": 0.69,
          "uncertainty": "Not specified",
          "unit": "dimensionless",
          "role": "Empirical prefactor adjusting the small-marble model to match data.",
          "anchors": [
            {
              "line_start": 122,
              "line_end": 122,
              "support": "Eq. (model_small) predicts the small-Ω data with a prefactor of 0.69."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "anchors": [
        {
          "line_start": 117,
          "line_end": 117,
          "support": "Small marbles: Ω≈4πR^3/3, l~R^2/a, S≈2πRl, δϵ≈δx/l."
        },
        {
          "line_start": 118,
          "line_end": 121,
          "support": "Gives α≈(6π^2)^{1/3}(a^3/Ω)^{2/3} μ f(φ)/(1-f(φ))."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "mechanism_id": "logistic_f_phi",
      "statement": "The dimensionless intergrain force function f(φ) follows a logistic function of the particle surface fraction, with an inflection point near close packing and onset near the 2D percolation threshold.",
      "equations": [
        "f(φ) = 1 / (1 + exp(-β(φ - φ_c)))",
        "φ_c = φ_o - (1/β) ln(γ/γ_eff(φ_o) - 1)"
      ],
      "variable_names": [
        "f(φ)",
        "φ",
        "β",
        "φ_c",
        "φ_o",
        "γ",
        "γ_eff"
      ],
      "parameters": [
        {
          "name": "beta_marbles",
          "value": 15.4,
          "uncertainty": "±1.7 (standard error from fit)",
          "unit": "dimensionless",
          "role": "Steepness parameter of the logistic function for liquid marbles.",
          "anchors": [
            {
              "line_start": 155,
              "line_end": 155,
              "support": "α/α_o = exp[β(φ-φ_o)] with β=15.4±1.7."
            },
            {
              "line_start": 556,
              "line_end": 556,
              "support": "Table: lycopodium marbles β=15.4±1.7."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "phi_c_marbles",
          "value": 0.9,
          "uncertainty": "±0.01",
          "unit": "dimensionless",
          "role": "Inflection point of the logistic function for liquid marbles.",
          "anchors": [
            {
              "line_start": 164,
              "line_end": 164,
              "support": "φ_c ≈ 0.90 ± 0.01."
            },
            {
              "line_start": 556,
              "line_end": 556,
              "support": "Table: lycopodium marbles φ_c=90±1%."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "anchors": [
        {
          "line_start": 159,
          "line_end": 164,
          "support": "From experimental result and Eq. (model_large) in asymptotic limit, f(φ)=1/(1+exp(-β(φ-φ_c))) with φ_c=φ_o-(1/β)ln(γ/γ_eff(φ_o)-1) ≈0.90±0.01."
        },
        {
          "line_start": 168,
          "line_end": 169,
          "support": "Yielding increases from φ≈0.65 near 2D percolation threshold 0.676; inflection at φ_c≈0.90 close to close-packing 0.907."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "mechanism_id": "raft_yielding_force",
      "statement": "In two-dimensional granular rafts, the force required to yield the raft with a dragged fiber scales with the intergrain force function f(φ), which follows a logistic form.",
      "equations": [
        "F_y = k δ",
        "F_y ~ q_y ~ f(φ)",
        "f(φ) = F_y(φ) / F_y^max"
      ],
      "variable_names": [
        "F_y",
        "k",
        "δ",
        "q_y",
        "f(φ)",
        "φ"
      ],
      "parameters": [],
      "anchors": [
        {
          "line_start": 177,
          "line_end": 179,
          "support": "Fiber deflection δ gives yielding force F_y=kδ; expected F_y~q_y~f(φ); normalized f(φ)=F_y/F_y^max."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
